SUMMARY:Teen Sleuths: Treachery at Tudor Mansion
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T150000
UID:77e6a666baff5154b1178c76142245eb@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Gaming\, Summer Reading\, Teens\n\nYou and your friends have b
 een invited to a prestigious dinner with Boddy Black for a chance to discu
 ss personal business. Shortly into the feast\, Boddy tells you all that he
  intends to blackmail all of you. The power immediately cuts out. When the
  lights come back on\, Boddy is dead! It is now up to you and your guests 
 to determine the who\, what\, and where of Boddy's murder... before it is 
 too late.Registration for Teen Sleuths: Treachery at Tudor Mansion will op
 en at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 24th for Manheim Township and East Lampet
 er residents and on Wednesday\, July 1st for residents of other municipali
 ties.This program is for teens ages 13-18 years only. Cancellations- Pleas
 e check your email prior to departing to verify that the program has not b
 een cancelled. Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to canc
 el their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be 
 restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one month
 ’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the 
 start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notified
  of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10
  minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other 
 circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At 
 this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will
  be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the p
 rogram. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5
  minutes past the start time.Drop Off Program – This program is intended
  for children over the age of 13 years who can participate independently. 
 Adult(s) must be present to check in child with youth services staff prior
  to program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space. Check In - All
  participants must provide an emergency contact number upon registration o
 r at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-sleuths-treachery-t
 udor-mansion-175153
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
