DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Tweens\, Teens\n\nLearning Robotics with Arts and Craft
 s for ages 10-14 This arts and crafts program combines creativity with eng
 ineering as participants explore basic robotics through hands-on projects.
  Participants will develop problem-solving skills\, ignite their curiosity
 \, and gain an introductory understanding of robotics - all within a fun a
 nd creative environment.The program provides practical experience in const
 ructing robotic creations and lays a foundation for future exploration and
  potential careers in the dynamic\, rapidly evolving field of robotics. Pa
 rticipants will also have an opportunity to drive one of our robots and le
 arn more about FIRST robotics programs. We'll have new projects\, so past 
 participants are encouraged to join us again.This program is led by FIRST 
 Tech Challenge Team 25650 - One Small Step for an Axolotl\, an all-girls r
 obotics team that won the 2026 Pennsylvania State Championship and earned 
 recognition at the FIRST World Championship. Girls are especially encourag
 ed to participate!
