SUMMARY:What Teeth Tell Us by Lancaster County Parks
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260707T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260707T140000
UID:2bab9669e83884d38ce1419e475293d1@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\, Teens\n\nMost dinosaurs a
 re known for their incredible teeth! By studying their teeth alone\, scien
 tists can decide what each type ate for dinner whether it be meat\, plants
 \, or a little bit of everything. In modern times we still use the teeth i
 n animals’ skulls to learn a lot about them. Join a Naturalist to read t
 he book “Tooth by Tooth” by Sara Levine\, discover the science of teet
 h and what they can tell us\, and finally try your hand at identifying sku
 lls to figure out what certain mystery animals like to have for dinner.
 😁This program was designed for children\, tweens\, and teens. *For the 
 safety and supervision of all participants: Children under 8 years old mus
 t be accompanied by an adult throughout the program. Children ages 8 and o
 lder are welcome to attend the program independently.  Registration for Wh
 at Teeth Tell Us by Lancaster County Parks will open at 9:00AM on Wednesda
 y\, June 24th for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wedn
 esday\, July 1st for residents of other municipalities.Library Program Pol
 icies Registration Requirements:  Please register ONLY the children who wi
 ll be attending.    No Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registra
 tion for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from r
 egistering for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please 
 cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the progr
 am to allow those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in re
 gistration status. Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior 
 to the start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. 
 The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, you
 r spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted ent
 ry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However
 \, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes pa
 st the start time. Cancellations- Please check your email prior to departi
 ng to verify that the program has not been cancelled. Photography - The Ma
 nheim Township Public Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographi
 ng or video recording individuals (including children) without their conse
 nt (or in the case of a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center BC
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/what-teeth-tell-us-lanca
 ster-county-parks-170756
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
