BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Figlancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/art-and-books-wild-robot-grades-1-3-at-pcad/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:figlancaster
X-SOURCE:Fig Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T160000
DTSTAMP:20260319T133041Z
CREATED:20260319T125736Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260319T133041Z
UID:10014530-1783517400-1783526400@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:Art and Books: Wild Robot: Grades 1-3 at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:The Wild Robot is a beloved children’s book (and now film!) which follows a curious robot called Roz\, who finds herself stranded in the wild on an island. Roz must learn to survive and earn the trust of the island’s animals. This is a beautiful tale of acceptance\, friendship and what it means to care about others. In this workshop for grades 1-3\, we will look at the pen and ink illustrations in the original book and explore themes from the book through various media! Come join us! This is a studio based class with lots of guidance to start followed by one-on-one instruction. Expect to have lots of creative freedom within the bounds of the assignment! \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/art-and-books-wild-robot-grades-1-3-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/03/W2-Robot-01.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Figlancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/how-to-start-a-sketchbook-grades-4-6-at-pcad/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:figlancaster
X-SOURCE:Fig Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T160000
DTSTAMP:20260319T133018Z
CREATED:20260319T130557Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260319T133018Z
UID:10014531-1783517400-1783526400@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:How to Start a Sketchbook! Grades 4-6 at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:In this playful\, hands-on\, class for students in grades 4-6 we will explore inventive tips\, tricks\, and techniques for breaking in a brand-new sketchbook with confidence. Using a variety of unexpected and creative materials\, you’ll prep\, experiment on\, and start multiple pages—embracing process over perfection. Inspired by the spirit of “Wreck This Journal\,” we’ll explore bold marks\, layered textures\, and imaginative prompts that free you from the pressure of the blank page. By the end of class\, you’ll leave with a sketchbook full of dynamic beginnings—rich with ideas\, energy\, and inspiration to keep creating long after the workshop ends. This is a studio based class with lots of guidance to start followed by one-on-one instruction. Expect to have lots of creative freedom within the bounds of the assignment! \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/how-to-start-a-sketchbook-grades-4-6-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/03/W2-Sketchbook-01.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Figlancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/comics-crashcourse-grades-6-9-at-pcad/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:figlancaster
X-SOURCE:Fig Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T160000
DTSTAMP:20260320T193526Z
CREATED:20260319T134946Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T193526Z
UID:10014532-1783517400-1783526400@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:Comics Crashcourse: Grades 6-9 at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:Comic books bring visually striking illustration to life with creative writing and pages upon pages of panels that take readers through vast worlds and detailed stories. The art of making comics is just as intricate and exciting. Have you ever wished you could bring your stories to life through the art of comics? If you enjoy creative writing\, character building\, and storyboarding this class is the perfect place for you to combine those skills and learn something new! Join us as we create our own short comics from the ground up and learn the basics of what it takes become your very own indie comic creator. This is a studio based class for students in grades 6-9 with some lecture\, lots of guidance\, and demonstration. Expect to have lots of creative freedom within the bounds of the assignment! \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/comics-crashcourse-grades-6-9-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/03/W2-Comics-Crashcourse-01.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/ameri-ca-dabra-erick-hershey-170345"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Ameri-Ca-Dabra with Erick Hershey
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260708T143000
UID:c1c0f592fb64a1c4397aa2f8619e4281@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Everyone\n\nThe Magic of Erick Hershey proudl
 y present our educational magic show\, “Ameri-ca-dabra!”\, an inspirin
 g and fun journey through the founding of our great nation. Told through e
 ntertaining and amazing magic\, this interactive show brings to life many 
 of the important places\, heroic people\, and foundational documents that 
 forged our nation.George Washington\, Betsy Ross\, Paul Revere\, the Decla
 ration of Independence\, the Liberty Bell\, and the history of our America
 n Flags\, all come to life through magic!Program held at St. John's Evange
 lical Lutheran Church in their Fellowship Hall. Please enter on the 6th st
 reet side at the red doors.Part of our 2026 Summer Reading program series.
LOCATION:Columbia
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/ameri-ca-dabra-erick-her
 shey-170345
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
