BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/learning-robotics-arts-and-crafts-178704"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Learning Robotics with Arts and Crafts
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T193000
UID:cf6df002706e2c4c036acd4af5f370b3@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Tweens\n\nLearning Robotics with Arts 
 and Crafts for ages 10-14This arts and crafts program combines creativity 
 with engineering as participants explore basic robotics through hands-on p
 rojects. Participants will develop problem-solving skills\, ignite their c
 uriosity\, and gain an introductory understanding of robotics—all within
  a fun and creative environment. The program provides practical experience
  in constructing robotic creations and lays a foundation for future explor
 ation and potential careers in the dynamic\, rapidly evolving field of rob
 otics. Participants will also have an opportunity to drive one of our robo
 ts and learn more about FIRST robotics programs. We'll have new projects\,
  so past participants are encouraged to join us again.This program is led 
 by FIRST Tech Challenge Team 25650 - One Small Step for an Axolotl\, an al
 l-girls robotics team that won the 2026 Pennsylvania State Championship an
 d earned recognition at the FIRST World Championship. Girls are especially
  encouraged to participate!Please note: Projects will be new for 2026 Summ
 er Robotics Camp and past participants are encouraged to join again.Regist
 ration for Learning Robotics with Arts and Crafts will open at 9:00AM on W
 ednesday\, July 1st for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and o
 n Wednesday\, July 8th for residents of other municipalities.Cancellations
 - Please check your email prior to departing to verify that the program ha
 s not been cancelled. Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing 
 to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month w
 ill be restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one
  month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior t
 o the start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to be no
 tified of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arr
 ive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and 
 other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated tim
 e. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list wh
 o will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into
  the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the pro
 gram 5 minutes past the start time.Drop Off Program – This program is in
 tended for children over the age of 6 years who can participate independen
 tly. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with youth services staff 
 prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space. Designate
 d Ages – Please adhere to the age restrictions designated on your regist
 ration. Only children in that age range will be admitted.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center C
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/learning-robotics-arts-a
 nd-crafts-178704
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
