 eir bee business. We will decorate upcycled pre-painted metal cans and ins
 tall paper tubes and a hanger to make a bee house to hang in your own gard
 en or yard. This program is designed for children ages 6 - 9 years old.  D
 esignated Ages – Please adhere to the age restrictions designated on y
 our registration. Only children in that age range will be admitted.   
 Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 30th for Manheim Town
 ship and East Lampeter residents and on Friday day\, July 3rd for resident
 s of other municipalities.Drop Off Program – This program is intended 
 for children over the age of 6 years who can participate independently. Ad
 ult(s) must be present to check in child with youth services staff prior t
 o program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space.  *For children
  ages 6–7\, this is a drop-off program\; however\, a parent or caregiv
 er must remain in the library for the duration of the program. Library P
 rogram Policies No Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration
  for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from regis
 tering for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please canc
 el your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program t
 o allow those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in regist
 ration status. Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to t
 he start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The 
 program will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your sp
 ot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. 
 If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, r
 egistrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past t
 he start time. Photography - The Manheim Township Public Library Code of C
 onduct Policy prohibits photographing or video recording individuals (incl
 uding children) without their consent (or in the case of a child\, the con
 sent of a parent or guardian).
