BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/workin-railroad-railroad-museum-pa-166985"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Workin' on the Railroad with the Railroad Museum of PA
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T113000
UID:5a78215c9d0ae82ac43a01a43058b60a@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nAll aboard for a journey
  into the world of railroads! The Railroad Museum of Pennsylvania is bring
 ing its engaging Workin’ on the Railroad program to our library this sum
 mer. Families are invited to explore the fascinating jobs that kept the tr
 ains running—from conductors and engineers to signalmen and porters.Part
 icipants will get hands-on with real railroad tools\, lanterns\, uniform i
 tems\, dining car china\, ticket punches\, and more! This interactive prog
 ram offers a unique opportunity to connect with history through touchable 
 artifacts and fun stories about life on the rails.Ideal for school-age chi
 ldren (Ages 7-12) and their families\, this program is perfect for curious
  minds who love trains\, history\, and hands-on learning.Registration for 
 Workin' on the Railroad presented by the Railroad Museum of Pennsylvania w
 ill open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 1st for Manheim Township and East L
 ampeter residents and on Wednesday\, July 8th for residents of other munic
 ipalities.Registration Requirements – To help us manage our space\, plea
 se register every person who will be attending\, including adults or sibli
 ngs.*For the safety and supervision of all participants: Children under 8 
 years old must be accompanied by an adult throughout the program. Children
  ages 8 and older are welcome to attend the program independently.  Librar
 y Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration
  for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from regis
 tering for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please canc
 el your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program t
 o allow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in re
 gistration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the 
 start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The pro
 gram will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot 
 will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If 
 spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, regi
 strants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the star
 t time.Cancellations- Please check your email prior to departing to verify
  that the program has not been cancelled. Photography - The Manheim Townsh
 ip Public Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video 
 recording individuals (including children) without their consent (or in th
 e case of a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center AB
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/workin-railroad-railroad
 -museum-pa-166985
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
