DESCRIPTION:Health & Wellness\, Summer Reading\, Children\n\nMini Chef Mor
 nings with GIANT\, a fun and interactive nutrition program for children 4 
 to 5 years old! This engaging program will introduce young learners to the
  importance of healthy eating through hands-on activities and simple\, nut
 ritious recipes.Guided by GIANT’s registered dietitian\, Miss Charlotte\
 , children will explore fresh ingredients\, learn how to make balanced foo
 d choices\, and create delicious\, easy-to-make snacks.  Program Highlight
 s:✅ Hands-on recipe demonstrations with kid-friendly ingredients✅ Nutr
 ition lessons tailored for young learners✅ Take-home educational materia
 ls for families to learn together Join us for this exciting opportunity to
  empower young minds with the knowledge and skills to make healthy choices
 —one tasty bite at a time!Join us for this exciting opportunity to empow
 er young minds with the knowledge and skills to make healthy choices—one
  tasty bite at a time! Let’s get cooking and learning together! 🥕🍎
 🥦Registration for Mini Chef with Giant Food Stores will open at 9:00AM 
 on Wednesday\, July 1st for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents a
 nd on Wednesday\, July 8th for residents of other municipalities.Adults at
 tending with their child(ren) do NOT need to register. Please add any addi
 tional registrants to your registration if more than one child that will b
 e participating in the program.Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons
  failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in 
 a month will be restricted from registering for future programs for a peri
 od of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hour
 s prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list
  to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – P
 lease arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for par
 king and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the desig
 nated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wai
 t list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be all
 owed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to ente
 r the program 5 minutes past the start time.Accompanying Adults – This p
 rogram is for adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to attend
  and be engaged with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted.Cancellat
 ions- Please check your email prior to departing to verify that the progra
 m has not been cancelled.Designated Ages – Please adhere to the age rest
 rictions designated on your registration. Only children in that age range 
 will be admitted.Photography - The Manheim Township Public Library Code of
  Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video recording individuals (in
 cluding children) without their consent (or in the case of a child\, the c
 onsent of a parent or guardian).
