UID:17c397fbdf1b6f42d5396aaf88c2547d@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Community\, Discussion\, STEM\, Summer Reading
 \, Tweens\n\nGet ready to build\, create\, and bring robots to life!This a
 wesome hands-on program is led by First Tech Challenge Team 25650\, "Dash\
 , One Small Step for an Axolotl"—an all-girls robotics team that had a r
 emarkable year\, winning the 2026 Pennsylvania State Championship and comp
 eting at the FIRST World Championship! Girls are especially encouraged to 
 come hang out and create with us.If you love arts\, crafts\, and inventing
 \, this program is for you. We’re combining total creativity with engine
 ering to explore the basics of robotics. Through epic hands-on projects\, 
 you’ll tackle fun challenges\, ignite your curiosity\, and learn how rob
 ots actually work—all in a super fun\, creative space. It’s the perfec
 t way to get real-world experience building your own robotic creations and
  see where a future in the fast-paced world of tech can take you.The best 
 part? You’ll get to drive one of our robots and find out how you can get
  involved in FIRST robotics.Bonus: We have brand-new projects lined up\, s
 o if you’ve been to one of our sessions before\, come back and join the 
 fun again!
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Break-out Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/learning-robotics-arts-c
 rafts-186425
