 very and create a story that fits its life. The Naturalist will tell the b
 eginning of a dinosaur story. When the Naturalist stops in the middle of t
 he story\, the participants will be asked to hunt for and find the parts o
 f dinosaurs hidden in the area. As they find the parts\, the group will be
  challenged to piece the dinosaur back together. Each group acts out an en
 d to the story using the dinosaur they have found\, making the story appro
 priate to the life of the dinosaur they have pieced together. Afterwards\,
  we will use a silly facts activity to challenge everyone’s dinosaur exp
 ertise. Ages 6-9.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH Multipurpose Room
