SUMMARY:Yes\, Lancaster was the U.S. Capital for a day!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T190000
UID:d336cee5af9eee10045c849f89f9e542@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Discussion\, Summer Reading\, Teens\, Adults\, Sen
 iors\n\nBest for adults and older youth. Please register every person in y
 our group!As we celebrate the nation's 250th birthday this summer\, we tur
 n to local history that shines a light on the role our community played in
  the nation's founding. On September 27\, 1777\, Lancaster briefly became 
 the nation’s capital when members of the Continental Congress fled Phila
 delphia and convened in the courthouse at what is now Penn Square.Adam Zur
 n\, the creator of Uncharted Lancaster\, is a local educator who offers ex
 citing and engaging adventures that teach local history to young and old. 
 He also will be selling books and curios after the event that will help su
 pport our library.
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/hold-uncharted-lanc-adul
 ts-159747
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
