BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-book-talk-156959"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Teen Book Talk: Summer of Broken Rules
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T190000
UID:c3f3167026f6579542431db562d687e2@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Teens\n\nFor Teens ages 13-18 years of age only.Ca
 lling all teen readers! Join us for Teen Book Talk\, a fun and engaging mo
 nthly book discussion group led by members of our Teen Advisory Board! Boo
 k selections are chosen by teens during advisory meetings. Interested in j
 oining the Teen Advisory Board? Sign up through the library calendar. Each
  month\, we’ll dive into a new title—ranging from trending young adult
  fiction to graphic novels\, fantasy epics\, thought-provoking contemporar
 y stories\, and more.This month we'll be reading "Sumer of Broken Rules" b
 y K.L. Walther.  Even though she is still grieving the death of her sister
 \, eighteen-year-old Meredith Fox plans to reconnect with family and frien
 ds when they gather on Martha's Vineyard for her cousin's big wedding - un
 less she gets distracted by a week - long game of Assassin and a handsome 
 groomsman. You’ll get the chance to share your thoughts\, hear different
  perspectives\, and connect with fellow book lovers in a relaxed and welco
 ming space. Snacks will be provided\, and occasionally we’ll have themed
  activities or giveaways tied to the book!Note: To help everyone stay pres
 ent and get the most out of the experience\, we ask that all phones stay i
 n pockets or bags during the program. Thank you for your cooperation!Libra
 ry Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registratio
 n for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from regi
 stering for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please can
 cel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program 
 to allow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in r
 egistration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the
  start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The pr
 ogram will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot
  will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If
  spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, reg
 istrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the sta
 rt time.Check In - All participants must provide an emergency contact numb
 er upon registration or at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-book-talk-156959
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/swoon-squad-romance-tbr-book-club-176852"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Swoon Squad: A Romance TBR Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T200000
UID:0780bf1fe451ebd5e266b4d46a02e8c2@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nSwoon Squad is a romance-cente
 red book club with a twist. Instead of everyone reading the same assigned 
 title\, we choose a monthly trope and invite you to pick any book that fit
 s the theme! Whether you're into sweet contemporary rom-coms\, high-heat h
 istorical reads\, or paranormal romance\, there's a seat for you at our ta
 ble! How it Works: Pick Your Own Adventure: We announce the month's trope\
 , and you choose a book from your own TBR pile or the library shelves that
  features it. Low Pressure\, High Fun: No more scrambling to finish a spec
 ific book you might not even like. Read at your own pace and bring your ho
 nest thoughts! The Discussion: We gather to swap recommendations\, vent ab
 out our favorite (and least favorite) clichés\, and discover new authors 
 through each other's picks.Come ready to share your pick\, discuss the tro
 pes\, and meet fellow romance fans in a comfortable library setting ❤️
 June 29 - ⚔️Enemies to Lovers ⚔️July 27 - 🥰😠Grumpy/Sunshine
 😠🥰August 31 - 🏆Sports Romance🏆September 28 - 📖Academic Roma
 nce📖October 26 - 🧛Paranormal Romance🧛November 30 - 🛏️Forced 
 Proximity🛏️December 28 - 🎁Holiday Romance🎁
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Patio
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/swoon-squad-romance-tbr-
 book-club-176852
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/cooks-books-history-plate-160160"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Cooks & Books: History on a Plate
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T193000
UID:e40bdccbf279678c1e3e03e3f6940a27@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Discussion\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nDust off your apr
 ons and your history books! This month\, Cooks & Books is traveling back i
 n time with Max Miller’s Tasting History. From Roman honey cakes to Vict
 orian sweets\, we’re recreating the flavors of the past to see if they t
 ruly stand the test of time. Don't see anything you want to make in the bo
 ok Tasting History? Check out Max Miller's hundreds of other videos and re
 cipes on YouTube!Pam Stoner from Historic Rock Ford will be on hand to tal
 k about 18th century foodways!🍽️Cooks & Books is an opportunity for p
 assionate home cooks to gather around the table for conversation over a po
 tluck feast of delicious food made from the recipes of a featured chef\, f
 ood blog\, or cookbook. Why not invite a friend to join you? The more\, th
 e merrier!Attendees\, who should be 14 years of age or older\, are asked t
 o bring a dish to share. Vegan/vegetarian recipes are welcome. Please brin
 g your own serving utensils\, place setting\, to-go container\, and bevera
 ge.New and experienced cooks are welcome! The event is free\, but reservat
 ions are required!
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/cooks-books-history-plat
 e-160160
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
