SUMMARY:Pennsylvania Wildlife Presented by Miller's Wildlife
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260728T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260728T113000
UID:e602ac0328a379e2675a3f258034441b@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Everyone\n\nHow well do you know your wild ne
 ighbors? Pennsylvania is famous for its extensive forests\, but you don't 
 have to go deep into the woods to learn about your wild neighbors! During 
 our Pennsylvania Wildlife program\, Patrick will introduce you to several 
 Pennsylvania native birds and reptiles - some of which\, you may find in y
 our own backyard! From the skies of downtown Harrisburg to the farmlands o
 f Lancaster County\, each ecosystem has its own important wildlife to appr
 eciate and protect. Join us as we discuss the ways that you can keep Penns
 ylvania's wilderness vast and diverse!Due to Pennsylvania Game Laws\, part
 icipants attending the program are NOT permitted to touch the animals at a
 ny time. Program will be held at St. John's Evangelical Lutheran Church. P
 lease enter on the 6th Street side at the RED Doors.Part of our 2026 Summe
 r Reading program series. Program sponsored by Brightspeed Fiber Internet.
LOCATION:Columbia
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/pennsylvania-wildlife-pr
 esented-millers-wildlife-170361
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
