BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/harry-potter-care-magical-creatures-101-167868"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Harry Potter: Care of Magical Creatures 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T113000
UID:dfebe1987261018c7783d779c443ac40@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Toddlers\, Children\, Tweens\, Teens\n\nThe C
 are of Magical Creatures program is conducted by Critter Connections. The 
 program covers a wide array of magical creatures\, ranging from the famili
 ar to the exotic. Students learn about their habitats\, behaviors\, magica
 l properties\, and how to interact with them safely. This is a fascinating
  course within the wizarding curriculum\, typically offered at magical ins
 titutions such as Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry. You will lea
 rn about snakes\, toads\, bearded dragons\, and many more.Registration for
  Harry Potter: Care of Magical Creatures 101 will open at 9:00AM on Wednes
 day\, July 15th for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on We
 dnesday\, July 22nd for residents of other municipalities.Registration Req
 uirements – To help us manage our space\, please register every person w
 ho will be attending\, including adults or siblings.*For the safety and su
 pervision of all participants: Children under 8 years old must be accompan
 ied by an adult throughout the program. Children ages 8 and older are welc
 ome to attend the program independently.  Cancellations- Please check your
  email prior to departing to verify that the program has not been cancelle
 d. Library Policies:No Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registrati
 on for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from reg
 istering for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please ca
 ncel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program
  to allow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in 
 registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to th
 e start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The p
 rogram will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spo
 t will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. I
 f spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, re
 gistrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the st
 art time.Photography - The Manheim Township Public Library Code of Conduct
  Policy prohibits photographing or video recording individuals (including 
 children) without their consent (or in the case of a child\, the consent o
 f a parent or guardian).
