DESCRIPTION:Gaming\, Summer Reading\, Teens\n\nDuring your stay on the lux
 urious Lady Marigold II\, a storm rolls in. As the storm rages on\, you fi
 nd the captain of the yacht face down in the water! As conditions worsen\,
  you must escape the yacht and solve the captain's murder.Registration for
  Teen Sleuths: Sabotage on the High Seas will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\
 , July 22nd for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednes
 day\, July 29th for residents of other municipalities.This program is for 
 teens ages 13-18 years only.Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons fa
 iling to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a m
 onth will be restricted from registering for future programs for a period 
 of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours p
 rior to the start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to
  be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Plea
 se arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parkin
 g and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designat
 ed time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait l
 ist who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowe
 d into the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter t
 he program 5 minutes past the start time.Drop Off Program – This program
  is intended for children over the age of 13 years who can participate ind
 ependently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with youth services
  staff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space. Ch
 eck In - All participants must provide an emergency contact number upon re
 gistration or at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-sleuths-sabotage-hi
 gh-seas-175154
