SUMMARY:Live STEAM Demo with the Railroad Museum of PA
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T113000
UID:3c999a73705825f73c7db5d9dd624196@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\n\nAll aboard for a high-energy jour
 ney through the science of trains! In this live STEAM (Science\, Technolog
 y\, Engineering\, Art\, and Math) demonstration\, the Railroad Museum of P
 ennsylvania will fire up a working miniature steam engine to show how stea
 m power set the world in motion.With fascinating historic artifacts\, dram
 atic photos\, and cool visual aids\, participants will uncover the evoluti
 on of locomotion—from the hissing power of steam to the quiet force of e
 lectricity and the modern might of diesel-electric engines. It’s a fast-
 paced\, hands-on look at how trains helped shape the world—and the scien
 ce that keeps them moving!Ideal for school-age children (Ages 7-12) and th
 eir families\, this program is perfect for curious minds who love trains\,
  history\, and hands-on learning.*For the safety and supervision of all pa
 rticipants: Children under 8 years old must be accompanied by an adult thr
 oughout the program. Children ages 8 and older are welcome to attend the p
 rogram independently.  Registration for Live STEAM Demo presented by the R
 ailroad Museum of Pennsylvania will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 22n
 d for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, July
  29th for residents of other municipalities.Registration Requirements – 
  To help us manage our space\, please register every person who will be at
 tending\, including adults or siblings.Cancellations- Please check your em
 ail prior to departing to verify that the program has not been cancelled. 
 Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their regist
 ration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from
  registering for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Pleas
 e cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the pro
 gram to allow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change
  in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior t
 o the start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. T
 he program will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your
  spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entr
 y. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\
 , registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past th
 e start time.Photography - The Manheim Township Public Library Code of Con
 duct Policy prohibits photographing or video recording individuals (includ
 ing children) without their consent (or in the case of a child\, the conse
 nt of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/live-steam-demo-railroad
 -museum-pa-166987
