DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nThe LEGO Block Pa
 rty at the library is a fun and creative program where children ages 8-12 
 come together to build various creations using LEGO bricks. Participants o
 ften have the opportunity to work individually or in teams to design and c
 onstruct imaginative structures\, vehicles\, and scenes based on a theme o
 r their own imagination. The club typically fosters collaboration\, proble
 m-solving\, and fine motor skills while encouraging a love for building an
 d creativity. It's a great way for community members to socialize\, learn\
 , and have fun in a supportive environment.Registration for Lego Block Par
 ty will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 29th for Manheim Township and E
 ast Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, August 5th for residents of othe
 r municipalities.For youth ages 8-12 years of age only.Designated Ages –
  Please adhere to the age restrictions designated on your registration. 
 Only children in that age range will be admitted.   *Children ages 8 a
 nd older are welcome to attend the program independently. Cancellations- P
 lease check your email prior to departing to verify that the program has n
 ot been cancelled. Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to 
 cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will
  be restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one mo
 nth’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to t
 he start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notif
 ied of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive
  10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and oth
 er circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. 
 At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who w
 ill be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into th
 e program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the progra
 m 5 minutes past the start time.Check In - All participants must provide a
 n emergency contact number upon registration or at the start of the progra
 m.
