BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/ed-klein-flip-books-youth-162387"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Ed Klein: Flip Books for Youth
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260813T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260813T113000
UID:9ef8c5f1200309b6be4c27f5aa6d13d8@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nEver wondered how drawin
 gs come to life in the movies? Before Pixar and special effect\, animated 
 movies were made like a flip book! In this hands-on class\, join our maste
 r cartoonist\, Ed Klein\, who previously worked with Hanna Barbera creatin
 g some of the most beloved cartoons! Participants will discover how simple
  images\, when viewed in rapid sequence\, bring the illusion of movement. 
 Perfect for creative kids who love drawing or storytelling\, this program 
 combines art\, imagination\, and a little movie magic to bring characters 
 to life- one page at a time!As an active artist in the field of animation\
 , Ed has contributed to over three hundred television commercials\, five f
 ull-length animated feature films\, and numerous animated television speci
 als and educational films. As an active cartoon character artist and desig
 ner\, Ed has designed and illustrated toys\, games\, apparel\, jewelry\, a
 nd figurines for The Warner Bros. Studio Stores\, and The Disney Stores\, 
 as well as for independent licensees.Registration for "Flip Books for Yout
 h" will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 29th for Manheim Township and E
 ast Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, August 5th for residents of othe
 r municipalities.This program is for children ages 8-12.Drop Off Program 
 – This program is intended for children over the age of 8 years who can 
 participate independently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with
  youth services staff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the 
 event space. Designated Ages – Please adhere to the age restrictions des
 ignated on your registration. Only children in that age range will be admi
 tted.Cancellations- Please check your email prior to departing to verify t
 hat the program has not been cancelled. Library Program PoliciesNo Show 
 – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library p
 rograms in a month will be restricted from registering for future programs
  for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at l
 east 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the w
 aiting list to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arr
 ivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to al
 low for parking and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly a
 t the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those
  on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants
  may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permit
 ted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Photography - The M
 anheim Township Public Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photograph
 ing or video recording individuals (including children) without their cons
 ent (or in the case of a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/ed-klein-flip-books-yout
 h-162387
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
