UID:fe228228d91125bb7f2808a66cfacd67@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Music\, Babies\, Toddlers\, Children\, Tweens\, Teens\, Adults
 \n\nGet ready for a high-energy\, family-friendly concert with award-winni
 ng musician Steven Courtney! Known for his engaging songs\, positive messa
 ges\, and interactive performances\, Steven brings joy to audiences of all
  ages with his blend of rock\, folk\, and playful storytelling. Whether yo
 u're clapping along\, dancing in your seat\, or singing out loud\, this mu
 sical event promises fun for the whole family. Perfect for children ages 3
  and up and their caregivers. Don’t miss this toe-tapping\, smile-sparki
 ng celebration of music and imagination!*For the safety and supervision of
  all participants: Children under 8 years old must be accompanied by an ad
 ult throughout the program. Children ages 8 and older are welcome to atten
 d the program independently.  Registration for Saturday Songs and Smiles w
 ith Steven Courtney will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 29th for Manhe
 im Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, August 5th for 
 residents of other municipalities.Registration Requirements – To help us
  manage our space\, please register every person who will be attending\, i
 ncluding adults or siblings.Cancellations- Please check your email prior t
 o departing to verify that the program has not been cancelled. Library Pro
 gram PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for 
 more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registerin
 g for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel yo
 ur registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to all
 ow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in registr
 ation status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start
  of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program 
 will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will 
 be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots
  remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registran
 ts will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start tim
 e.Photography - The Manheim Township Public Library Code of Conduct Policy
  prohibits photographing or video recording individuals (including childre
 n) without their consent (or in the case of a child\, the consent of a par
 ent or guardian).
