BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Amtshows": "https://amtshows.com/show/the-billy-joel-legacy/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:amtshows
X-SOURCE:American Music Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T200000
DTSTAMP:20260705T000615
CREATED:20260608T133025Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260702T142013Z
UID:10001932-1789848000-1789848000@amtshows.com
SUMMARY:The Billy Joel Legacy
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: $39 $49 $59 $69\nAMT Member Pre-Sale: Wednesday\, June 10 at 10:00 a.m.\nPublic On-Sale: Friday\, June 12 at 10:00 a.m. \nClick Here to purchase VIP Experience \nThe Billy Joel Legacy VIP Experience Upgrade* $100\n\nA private 20-minute acoustic performance with the lead performer of The Billy Joel Legacy for VIP attendees only\, featuring exclusive Billy Joel songs not performed in the main show.\n\nA Meet & Greet and photo opportunity with the lead performer of The Billy Joel Legacy show.\n\nA limited edition\, collectible VIP laminate & lanyard\n\n*Upgrade packages DO NOT INCLUDE TICKETS. A ticket is required to enter the venue.\nExperience the music\, story\, and legacy of one of America’s most beloved singer-songwriters with The Billy Joel Legacy: Celebrating the Piano Man. From the producers of The Simon and Garfunkel Story and The Life and Music of George Michael\, this captivating concert event takes audiences on a journey through Billy Joel’s remarkable career—from his Long Island beginnings to international superstardom. Featuring faithful recreations of his greatest hits\, stunning multimedia visuals\, and engaging storytelling\, The Billy Joel Legacy brings classics like “Piano Man\,” “Uptown Girl\,” “We Didn’t Start the Fire\,” “New York State of Mind\,” and more to life on stage. Discover the stories behind the songs\, the moments that shaped the music\, and the enduring impact of an artist whose work continues to inspire generations. More than a tribute concert\, this is a heartfelt celebration of Billy Joel’s extraordinary contribution to music and culture. \nFor certain concerts\, audience members may prefer to stand or dance\, especially when encouraged by the artist to do so. Guest expectations differ\, so we simply ask all attendees to extend mutual respect toward one another and maintain awareness of those around them. Our staff will only intervene in matters of safety or when behavior is deemed unruly\, combative\, or disruptive to the overall performance.
URL:https://amtshows.com/show/the-billy-joel-legacy/
LOCATION:American Music Theatre\, 2425 Lincoln Hwy East\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17605\, United States
CATEGORIES:Celebrity Concerts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://amtshows.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/BJL_Concessions-Events-and-News-for-Website-1920x1080-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Amtshows": "https://amtshows.com/show/rhonda-vincent-with-the-malpass-brothers/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:amtshows
X-SOURCE:American Music Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T150000
DTSTAMP:20260705T000615
CREATED:20260323T133002Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260520T184459Z
UID:10001868-1789916400-1789916400@amtshows.com
SUMMARY:Rhonda Vincent with The Malpass Brothers
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: $29 $39 $49 $69 \nRhonda Vincent is a powerhouse performer whose fiery talent and unmistakable voice have made her one of the most celebrated artists in bluegrass music. Hailing from Greentop\, Missouri\, Rhonda’s musical roots run five generations deep. She began performing professionally at just five years old with her family’s band\, The Sally Mountain Show\, gaining early experience on stage\, radio\, and television. By her teens\, she had mastered multiple instruments and developed the work ethic and passion that would define her career. \nHer journey took a pivotal turn when a chance performance led to an invitation from the Grand Ole Opry—an early sign of the remarkable path ahead. Rhonda went on to build an award-winning career\, earning the title “New Queen of Bluegrass” and becoming known for her signature blend of traditional roots and contemporary energy. Her breakthrough album Back Home Again cemented her status as a leading voice in the genre. \nA Grammy Award winner and one of the most decorated artists in bluegrass history\, Rhonda Vincent has earned numerous honors\, including multiple International Bluegrass Music Association Female Vocalist of the Year awards and Entertainer of the Year. In 2021\, she achieved a lifelong dream with her official induction into the Grand Ole Opry. \nWith a voice that transcends genres and collaborations that include artists like Dolly Parton\, Rhonda Vincent continues to captivate audiences with high-energy performances\, world-class musicianship\, and a deep-rooted love of the music that started it all. \nAs young boys\, The Malpass Brothers – Christopher and Taylor – soaked up the music of their granddad’s phonograph records.  Christopher earned his first talent show trophy at age 7\, and Taylor was playing mandolin by the time he was 10.  Today\, they promote the work and music of classic country artists they treasure while creating new music and making their own mark in the lineage of a rich American cultural heritage.  With sincerity\, honesty\, and an utter ease on stage that belies their years\, their smooth vocal blend and skillful musicianship layer infectiously into the deep respect they pay to legends who have paved the way.  Add the funny\, off-the-cuff quips between the two 20-something siblings\, and the engaging concert becomes a magnetic time-traveling journey to when a calmer rhythm reigned supreme. \nFor certain concerts\, audience members may prefer to stand or dance\, especially when encouraged by the artist to do so. Guest expectations differ\, so we simply ask all attendees to extend mutual respect toward one another and maintain awareness of those around them. Our staff will only intervene in matters of safety or when behavior is deemed unruly\, combative\, or disruptive to the overall performance.
URL:https://amtshows.com/show/rhonda-vincent-with-the-malpass-brothers/
LOCATION:American Music Theatre\, 2425 Lincoln Hwy East\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17605\, United States
CATEGORIES:Celebrity Concerts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://amtshows.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/RVMB_Concessions-Events-and-News-for-Website-1920x1080-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
