SUMMARY:The Waldorf Effect: A Paranormal Research Theory
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T200000
UID:26d3f77b1209ac3d3489f3d1b3646b64@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nJoin author Lau
 rissa Mary Rex as she discusses the research behind her book The Waldorf E
 ffect: A Paranormal Research Theory.This four-part theory for understandin
 g hauntings\, developed through research at the Waldorf Estate of Fear\, p
 roposes that hauntings are generated by the interaction of controllable an
 d uncontrollable factors\, such as geology and history\, which influence e
 nvironmental changes and the energy dynamics of a location. The book combi
 nes data-driven and metaphysical approaches. Ages 18+ · Space is limited 
 · Registration required
LOCATION:Lancaster\, LPL Board Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/waldorf-effect-paranorma
 l-research-theory-153123
